# 16·%ctaid.x | ((%tid.x mod 16) − 4): on lanes 0 to 3 of every 16 the
# right side is negative and sets every bit above its low four, so the
# or is that side alone and ptxas, keeping the or, stores at param_0 − 16
# to − 4. It is no add: the right side may set any bit from 4 up, and
# the address is unknown.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/or_negative.ptx | FileCheck "%s"
CHECK: kernel micro_or_negative
CHECK: st.global.u32  global store 4 B
CHECK-SAME: unknown: or whose sides may both set bit 4
